{
  "dom_id": "step-q332324",
  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "A basketball player has a $70%$ chance of making a free throw on any given attempt. The player continues shooting free throws until they make a shot. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability that the player will attempt fewer than $4$ free throws is{{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "A geometric random variable $X$ with probability of success $p$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(1-p)^{x-1}p\n$$\n\nLet $X$ be the number of free throws attempted until the player made a shot. Since the chance of making a free throw is $70%,$ the number of free throws attempted until the player makes a shot can be modeled as a geometric random variable with a probability of success\n\n$$\np=70%=\\frac{70}{100}=0.7.\n$$\n\nSo, $X∼\\text{Geom}(0.7).$ In this case, $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =(1-0.7)^{x-1}(0.7) \\\\  & =(0.3)^{x-1}(0.7)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that the player will attempt fewer than $4$ free throws is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<4) & =P(X\\in \\{1,2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2)+f(3) \\\\  & =(0.3)^{0}(0.7)+(0.3)^{1}(0.7)+(0.3)^{2}(0.7) \\\\  & =0.7+0.21+0.063 \\\\  & =0.973.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [
    {
      "key": "field-1",
